    "content": "The 2026 NCAA Division I Men's Wrestling Championships will be held March 19–21 at Rocket Mortgage FieldHouse in Cleveland, Ohio. This premier three-day tournament determines NCAA Division I All-Americans and national champions across ten weight classes, with 330 total wrestlers competing. 2026 NCAA DI Men's Wrestling Championships Details: Dates: Thursday, March 19 – Saturday, March 21, 2026. Location: Rocket Mortgage FieldHouse in Cleveland, Ohio. Schedule (Eastern Time): Thursday, March 19: Preliminaries (12 p.m.), Preliminaries and wrestle-backs (7 p.m.). Friday, March 20: Quarterfinals and wrestle-backs (12 p.m.), Semifinals and wrestle-backs (8 p.m.). Saturday, March 21: Championship Finals. Coverage: Events are typically televised on the ESPN family of networks, often streaming on ESPN+. The tournament features 330 wrestlers from 76 teams, with 33 wrestlers in each of the ten weight classes (125 pounds to Heavyweight). Brackets and seeds for the 2026 championships were announced on March 11, 2026, following the release of at-large qualifiers on March 10. Recent Performance and Context: Penn State entered the tournament after a dominant performance at the 2026 Big Ten Championships, where they won seven individual titles. Oklahoma State and Ohio State are among the top contenders for the 2026 team title alongside Penn State. Oklahoma State holds the record for most team titles, with 34, according to Wikipedia. Other Divisions (2026): DII: The 2026 Division II Wrestling Championships took place March 13–14 at the Denny Sanford PREMIER Center in Sioux Falls, SD. DIII: The 2026 Division III Wrestling Championships were held in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, where Wartburg clinched their 17th team title on March 14, according to USA Wrestling.",
